LQR_ORIG (faithful port of Bisevac et al. 2026, Algorithm 1): per flooder, dt 0.5 s = every 2nd 0.25 s tick, CPU = vhost thread % of one core over that 0.5 s window, median of last 5, CPU_eff = 0.7 smooth + 0.3 (smooth + trend), u = -K [e, edot], soft limit margin 0.5 (exp 0.5 inside, 0.7 above), clip [0, 0.95], nearest of 20 levels; actuator xdp_dropfrac.o (drop iff (total x drop_bp) % 10000 < drop_bp), swapped in on the 4 flooders for the slot and xdp_limit back after it; PPS feed-forward of the public v2 code LEFT OUT (not in Algorithm 1); management-port exemption NOT enabled; nothing tuned; exp43: re-identified K from the ARE on the ZOH discretisation of the authors' continuous model (exp42's Euler ARE on calib42 had the wrong sign), refused if K[0] >= 0
DEVIATION (lqr_orig only, documented): when the victims' window ends drop_bp is set to 0 on all flooders BEFORE waiting for the flooder iperf3 clients (their -J report and control channel cross the dropping vnet), with a 60 s timeout + WARNING on that wait; release time = column u_release_s (s after flooder launch); eBPF counters unaffected
